1
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:15,849
All right, let's start talking
about the last quest.

2
00:00:15,932 --> 00:00:17,976
You've worked so hard
on your quests so far.

3
00:00:18,059 --> 00:00:20,270
Only the last quest remains.

4
00:00:20,895 --> 00:00:22,647
We will reveal the final quest.

5
00:00:22,731 --> 00:00:23,815
The final quest is…

6
00:00:25,316 --> 00:00:28,194
Jirisan. Climbing this is the final quest.

7
00:00:28,278 --> 00:00:29,529
-Yeah.
-Congratulations!

8
00:00:29,612 --> 00:00:30,488
I saw it coming.

9
00:00:30,572 --> 00:00:32,157
Yeah, I knew this would happen.

10
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:34,534
I was wondering why
it hadn't shown up yet.

11
00:00:34,617 --> 00:00:36,619
CHEONWANGBONG PEAK

12
00:00:36,703 --> 00:00:40,874
JIRISAN MOUNTAIN

13
00:00:41,958 --> 00:00:45,045
THE ETERNAL FIXTURE
OF KOREA'S SOUTHERN END

14
00:00:47,213 --> 00:00:53,511
NESTLED WITHIN THE MOUNTAINS
STRETCHING FROM THE EAST TO THE WEST

15
00:00:55,764 --> 00:00:59,100
AND FEATURING CASCADING WATERFALLS

16
00:00:59,184 --> 00:01:02,103
IS KOREA'S FIRST NATIONAL PARK

17
00:01:04,272 --> 00:01:06,483
AND THE HIGHEST PEAK OF JIRISAN

18
00:01:08,359 --> 00:01:10,487
CHEONWANGBONG

19
00:01:14,866 --> 00:01:18,953
THE KOREAN SPIRIT AROSE FROM HERE

20
00:01:33,468 --> 00:01:35,678
THE PLACE ABOVE THE CLOUDS

21
00:01:35,762 --> 00:01:39,057
WHERE YOU CAN LOOK DOWN
ON THE MOUNTAINS AND RIVERS

22
00:01:40,225 --> 00:01:46,564
IT CONNECTS PEOPLE WITH NATURE

23
00:01:46,648 --> 00:01:49,692
AND THE EARTH WITH THE SKY

24
00:01:52,779 --> 00:01:56,783
THE SACRED MOUNTAIN
OF THE KOREAN PEOPLE, JIRISAN

25
00:01:56,866 --> 00:01:58,910
The mission is simple this time.

26
00:01:58,993 --> 00:02:01,704
The goal is to just reach Cheonwangbong.

27
00:02:01,788 --> 00:02:03,373
How high is it?

28
00:02:03,456 --> 00:02:05,750
CHEONWANGBONG IS 1,915 M ABOVE SEA LEVEL

29
00:02:05,834 --> 00:02:07,252
It's as high as Hallasan.

30
00:02:07,335 --> 00:02:10,463
SECOND TALLEST MOUNTAIN IN KOREA

31
00:02:10,547 --> 00:02:13,633
But I heard it takes longer than a day
to reach the top.

32
00:02:13,716 --> 00:02:16,010
THEY WILL HIKE A TRAIL
THAT TAKES LESS THAN A DAY

33
00:02:16,094 --> 00:02:18,263
That must've been a different trail then.

34
00:02:18,847 --> 00:02:21,641
I'd like an easy route so we can enjoy it.

35
00:02:21,724 --> 00:02:24,519
We want to appreciate the scenery,
so let us take an easy trail.

36
00:02:25,436 --> 00:02:29,649
But if it's for two days, will we relax
and rest on the first day as usual?

37
00:02:29,732 --> 00:02:31,234
Should we do some activities?

38
00:02:31,317 --> 00:02:32,986
Sure, we don't mind.

39
00:02:33,069 --> 00:02:35,989
But you might end up losing your gold.

40
00:02:36,072 --> 00:02:38,074
NO WAY

41
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:40,326
Let's leave all our gold at home.

42
00:02:40,410 --> 00:02:41,911
EXTREME MEASURES

43
00:02:41,995 --> 00:02:43,872
We understand. Let's wrap up for today.

44
00:02:43,955 --> 00:02:45,748
-Good work, everyone!
-Thank you!

45
00:02:45,832 --> 00:02:47,667
THEIR OFFICIAL COMMITMENTS IN ULSAN END

46
00:02:47,750 --> 00:02:49,460
THAT EVENING

47
00:02:50,336 --> 00:02:54,883
I'll count on you to make
something delicious, Mom.

48
00:02:56,426 --> 00:02:59,929
THE NEXT MORNING
AT THE YEONGNAM ALPS BASE CAMP

49
00:03:00,013 --> 00:03:01,848
We'll see you there.

50
00:03:01,931 --> 00:03:04,642
THEY VISIT TARZZAN'S PARENTS
FOR THE SEOLLAL HOLIDAY

51
00:03:05,226 --> 00:03:08,646
THEY GO TO DOWNTOWN ULSAN

52
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:13,192
Then, let's buy some fruit
and a red ginseng gift set.

53
00:03:13,276 --> 00:03:14,235
Sounds good.

54
00:03:14,319 --> 00:03:16,487
A gift set of health products
and a gift set of fruits.

55
00:03:17,572 --> 00:03:19,282
STRONG HOLIDAY VIBES

56
00:03:19,365 --> 00:03:20,658
-Hello.
-Hello.

57
00:03:20,742 --> 00:03:22,076
THEY ARRIVE AT A DEPARTMENT STORE

58
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:24,037
These red ginseng supplements are good.

59
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,079
-This?
-That's right.

60
00:03:25,163 --> 00:03:26,873
-Okay, let's get this one.
-One of these?

61
00:03:26,956 --> 00:03:28,124
-We'll take this one.
-Okay.

62
00:03:28,207 --> 00:03:29,918
His house is very close.

63
00:03:30,001 --> 00:03:31,753
-Really? Is that so?
-Yes.

64
00:03:31,836 --> 00:03:33,671
HEALTH SUPPLEMENT PURCHASE IS COMPLETE

65
00:03:33,755 --> 00:03:34,839
This one?

66
00:03:34,923 --> 00:03:36,299
-One of these.
-That's perfect.

67
00:03:36,382 --> 00:03:37,425
Let's get this one.

68
00:03:37,508 --> 00:03:39,344
This one. We'll take this one.

69
00:03:40,929 --> 00:03:42,889
I feel rather bad.

70
00:03:42,972 --> 00:03:44,849
THE BEST ONE WITHOUT HESITATION

71
00:03:44,933 --> 00:03:47,101
-Do you want to pay in installments?
-No, it's okay.

72
00:03:47,185 --> 00:03:49,646
THE OLDER MEMBERS BUY THE GIFTS
WITH THEIR OWN MONEY

73
00:03:50,438 --> 00:03:52,148
You guys spent too much.

74
00:03:52,232 --> 00:03:54,359
It's okay. We should do things right.

75
00:03:55,735 --> 00:03:59,822
THEY HEAD TO MEET TARZZAN'S PARENTS
WITH A TRUNK FULL OF GIFTS

76
00:04:01,115 --> 00:04:05,578
THEY ARRIVE AT TARZZAN'S HOUSE

77
00:04:06,663 --> 00:04:09,582
NOW THAT THEY'RE HERE,
THEY FEEL NERVOUS AND EXCITED

78
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:12,752
My heart's beating fast.

79
00:04:17,048 --> 00:04:19,300
-It smells delicious.
-I smell food.

80
00:04:19,384 --> 00:04:20,760
It smells like fancy food.

81
00:04:20,843 --> 00:04:21,761
Maybe pasta?

82
00:04:22,470 --> 00:04:24,973
CAN ALWAYS SMELL FOOD
IN THE HALLWAYS DURING THE HOLIDAYS

83
00:04:26,766 --> 00:04:28,851
-Hey, Chae-min, you go in first.
-What?

84
00:04:28,935 --> 00:04:30,770
You go in first. You're the most handsome.

85
00:04:30,853 --> 00:04:32,355
Right, you should enter first.

86
00:04:34,315 --> 00:04:35,733
-Hello.
-Hello.

87
00:04:35,817 --> 00:04:36,776
TARZZAN'S FATHER

88
00:04:36,859 --> 00:04:38,945
-Hello.
-Hi, Auntie.

89
00:04:39,028 --> 00:04:41,614
THEY ENTER TARZZAN'S PARENTS' HOUSE

90
00:04:41,698 --> 00:04:42,991
-Hello, ma'am.
-Hello.

91
00:04:43,074 --> 00:04:44,200
-Hello.
-Come on in.

92
00:04:44,867 --> 00:04:45,702
-Lee Chae-min?
-Yes.

93
00:04:45,785 --> 00:04:47,287
-Nice to meet you.
-Nice to meet you.

94
00:04:47,370 --> 00:04:49,122
Car, the garden? Nice to meet you.

95
00:04:49,205 --> 00:04:50,039
TARZZAN'S MOTHER

96
00:04:50,123 --> 00:04:51,165
Hello.

97
00:04:51,249 --> 00:04:52,917
-Dowoon of DAY6.
-Hello.

98
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:54,252
I've been enjoying your show.

99
00:04:54,335 --> 00:04:55,628
Thank you so much.

100
00:04:55,712 --> 00:04:56,754
-Hello.
-Hello.

101
00:04:56,838 --> 00:04:59,340
Wait, here's the person
we wanted to see the most.

102
00:04:59,424 --> 00:05:01,467
-Hello, Producer Nah.
-Hello.

103
00:05:01,551 --> 00:05:02,719
-Come on in.
-Please come in.

104
00:05:03,303 --> 00:05:05,805
-We brought some things.
-It's not much, but…

105
00:05:05,888 --> 00:05:07,265
Thank you so much.

106
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:11,853
Gosh, they prepared a lot of food for us.

107
00:05:11,936 --> 00:05:15,023
TARZZAN'S HOUSE REVEALED
FOR THE FIRST TIME

108
00:05:18,276 --> 00:05:20,445
-Let me introduce his aunt.
-I see. His aunt.

109
00:05:20,528 --> 00:05:21,446
INTRODUCING THE FAMILY

110
00:05:21,529 --> 00:05:22,530
That's Chae-won's aunt.

111
00:05:22,613 --> 00:05:24,073
TARZZAN'S AUNT

112
00:05:24,157 --> 00:05:25,199
-Hello.
-Hello.

113
00:05:25,283 --> 00:05:26,451
I'm helping out for the day.

114
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:29,787
Do you think I take after my mom or dad?

115
00:05:30,538 --> 00:05:33,207
Looking at you now,
your eyes and nose resemble your dad's.

116
00:05:33,291 --> 00:05:34,292
-You're right.
-Yes.

117
00:05:34,375 --> 00:05:37,128
TARZZAN'S DAD

118
00:05:37,211 --> 00:05:39,964
And the lower half of your face
resembles your mom.

119
00:05:40,048 --> 00:05:41,424
Especially your lips.

120
00:05:41,507 --> 00:05:44,260
TARZZAN'S MOM

121
00:05:44,343 --> 00:05:46,220
Hey, look at his photos.

122
00:05:46,846 --> 00:05:47,764
-Look.
-He's so cute.

123
00:05:47,847 --> 00:05:48,806
He's adorable.

124
00:05:48,890 --> 00:05:51,476
Hey, take a look at his hairstyle here.

125
00:05:52,101 --> 00:05:54,937
Hey, it looks good. It looks good on him.

126
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:56,731
He was handsome as a kid too.

127
00:05:56,814 --> 00:05:58,441
You look exactly the same.

128
00:05:58,524 --> 00:06:02,320
AGES 14, 6, 16, 18

129
00:06:02,403 --> 00:06:04,697
What is this? <i>Power Rangers Mystic Force?</i>

130
00:06:04,781 --> 00:06:05,948
He must've been in a play.

131
00:06:06,032 --> 00:06:07,241
He went to see the musical.

132
00:06:07,867 --> 00:06:08,868
So cute.

133
00:06:09,494 --> 00:06:11,079
This next room is mine.

134
00:06:11,829 --> 00:06:13,456
-Is this your room?
-Yes.

135
00:06:13,998 --> 00:06:15,833
-We left it as it was.
-You like this stuff?

136
00:06:15,917 --> 00:06:19,003
Well, it was my favorite stuffed animal
since I was little.

137
00:06:20,379 --> 00:06:23,091
PRODUCER NAH LOOKS AROUND TARZZAN'S ROOM

138
00:06:23,174 --> 00:06:25,218
Would you like to see his old diary?

139
00:06:26,219 --> 00:06:27,345
Come on, Mom!

140
00:06:28,054 --> 00:06:29,472
-His diary.
-No, you can't.

141
00:06:29,555 --> 00:06:31,182
Hold on. Where is his diary, ma'am?

142
00:06:31,265 --> 00:06:32,809
PRODUCER NAH HAS FOUND HIS TARGET

143
00:06:32,892 --> 00:06:34,102
-Where are they?
-Here.

144
00:06:34,185 --> 00:06:35,686
-Seriously…
-All of these?

145
00:06:35,770 --> 00:06:37,396
I told you to hide them.

146
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:38,981
Yes, here's his diary.

147
00:06:40,191 --> 00:06:41,734
His handwriting is good.

148
00:06:41,818 --> 00:06:43,903
"On the first day of sixth grade,

149
00:06:43,986 --> 00:06:48,366
Lee Dong-hyeok told me
that Ms. Kim Young-kyung is nice."

150
00:06:48,449 --> 00:06:50,284
"That made my palms so sweaty."

151
00:06:50,368 --> 00:06:52,120
-What does that mean?
-What does that mean?

152
00:06:52,954 --> 00:06:55,498
Why were you scared of your teacher?
Did you do something bad?

153
00:06:55,581 --> 00:06:57,375
-In sixth grade?
-I think so.

154
00:06:58,084 --> 00:06:59,293
Where should we sit?

155
00:06:59,377 --> 00:07:02,338
NOW THAT THEY'VE FINISHED THE TOUR,
IT'S TIME TO EAT

156
00:07:03,256 --> 00:07:05,758
-Is this sukiyaki?
-Yes.

157
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:07,593
What a fancy dish.

158
00:07:08,344 --> 00:07:10,888
I made these this morning.

159
00:07:11,597 --> 00:07:16,561
HOMEMADE SUKIYAKI MADE BY TARZZAN'S MOM

160
00:07:17,562 --> 00:07:20,940
BEEF JEON AND SHRIMP JEON SHE MADE HERSELF

161
00:07:21,607 --> 00:07:23,568
AND NOTICE THAT THE JEON
WAS MADE WITH SIRLOIN

162
00:07:23,651 --> 00:07:25,194
Thank you for the food, ma'am.

163
00:07:25,278 --> 00:07:26,654
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

164
00:07:26,737 --> 00:07:27,613
Sure thing.

165
00:07:28,906 --> 00:07:30,783
You should try the <i>jeon</i> first.

166
00:07:30,867 --> 00:07:32,368
-Okay.
-I'll give it a taste.

167
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:34,036
Thank you. Please go first.

168
00:07:35,955 --> 00:07:38,749
A BITE WITH FRESH KIMCHI

169
00:07:41,210 --> 00:07:43,504
YUM

170
00:07:43,588 --> 00:07:44,964
Thank you so much.

171
00:07:46,424 --> 00:07:49,469
Gosh, it's really good. Have some.

172
00:07:50,052 --> 00:07:52,555
How did she make it so flat?

173
00:07:54,974 --> 00:07:59,729
NOW IT'S TIME TO TRY THE SUKIYAKI

174
00:08:03,232 --> 00:08:04,484
This is a top-tier dish.

175
00:08:04,567 --> 00:08:06,694
DIPS IT INTO A RAW EGG AND TAKES A BITE

176
00:08:10,072 --> 00:08:11,824
Gosh, I feel so good.

177
00:08:18,289 --> 00:08:20,124
-You dip it into this, right?
-It's good.

178
00:08:20,625 --> 00:08:23,961
Actually, my second favorite dish
after pork cutlets is sukiyaki.

179
00:08:25,046 --> 00:08:27,340
Seriously. This is so good.

180
00:08:27,423 --> 00:08:31,552
The tyrant from <i>Bon Appétit, Your Majesty</i>
says it's delicious.

181
00:08:31,636 --> 00:08:32,678
It's really good.

182
00:08:32,762 --> 00:08:33,804
-Thank you.
-Seriously.

183
00:08:35,181 --> 00:08:37,350
-You've eaten this since you were little?
-Yes.

184
00:08:37,433 --> 00:08:39,852
Really? This must be
one of her best dishes.

185
00:08:39,936 --> 00:08:41,354
Since I did sports,

186
00:08:41,437 --> 00:08:44,273
I needed to find food
that was healthy and delicious,

187
00:08:44,357 --> 00:08:45,900
so I liked dishes like this.

188
00:08:45,983 --> 00:08:47,193
This is so good.

189
00:08:47,276 --> 00:08:48,819
-Goodness, there's also rice.
-Yes.

190
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:50,196
My goodness.

191
00:08:50,279 --> 00:08:52,031
We heard you didn't have breakfast.

192
00:08:52,114 --> 00:08:52,990
That's right.

193
00:08:53,074 --> 00:08:55,493
Tarzzan couldn't eat
because he woke up a bit late.

194
00:08:55,576 --> 00:08:57,620
TARZZAN'S MOM'S ABALONE RICE

195
00:08:57,703 --> 00:09:00,248
Is there anyone here
you were curious about?

196
00:09:00,331 --> 00:09:03,709
There are fans among the people I know.

197
00:09:03,793 --> 00:09:06,254
-Right.
-They asked me to get autographs for them.

198
00:09:06,337 --> 00:09:09,257
I mean, it's hard to even get
an autograph from my son.

199
00:09:09,924 --> 00:09:12,009
IT'S HARD TO SEE HER BUSY SON

200
00:09:12,093 --> 00:09:14,762
I guess you can't see your parents often.

201
00:09:14,845 --> 00:09:15,846
No.

202
00:09:15,930 --> 00:09:19,016
He said he has to work
throughout the holidays this year too.

203
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:20,726
I know.

204
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:23,271
Has Tarzzan ever given you a hard time?

205
00:09:26,524 --> 00:09:27,858
He's a good son.

206
00:09:28,359 --> 00:09:30,027
-My son's nice.
-Yes, he's so nice.

207
00:09:30,111 --> 00:09:31,696
I don't think he'd ever cause trouble.

208
00:09:31,779 --> 00:09:34,782
I got a call once
that he got hurt outside.

209
00:09:34,865 --> 00:09:36,450
While playing rough outside?

210
00:09:36,534 --> 00:09:38,369
-Yes.
-And he made you worried sick.

211
00:09:38,452 --> 00:09:39,412
Exactly.

212
00:09:39,495 --> 00:09:41,956
He went to the park on his own,
and they said he got hurt.

213
00:09:42,039 --> 00:09:44,750
I got hurt while going
to Ulsan Grand Park alone.

214
00:09:44,834 --> 00:09:46,752
By the way, yesterday,

215
00:09:46,836 --> 00:09:49,213
Tarzzan took us
to all of his favorite places.

216
00:09:49,297 --> 00:09:51,257
From the <i>milmyeon</i> place to the park.

217
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:52,174
Really?

218
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:58,055
By the way, who decided
on having lunch here today?

219
00:09:58,139 --> 00:09:59,724
Who planned it?

220
00:09:59,807 --> 00:10:01,183
THE PRESIDENT DID

221
00:10:01,267 --> 00:10:03,227
I wish he'd discussed it with us.

222
00:10:05,021 --> 00:10:07,148
Wait, we thought he'd told you beforehand.

223
00:10:07,231 --> 00:10:10,568
-I did tell you.
-He called me at 6:00 p.m. yesterday.

224
00:10:10,651 --> 00:10:12,069
-Yesterday afternoon?
-Yes.

225
00:10:12,153 --> 00:10:15,531
He said, "Mom, eight people
are coming at 1:00 p.m. tomorrow."

226
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:18,117
How many times did I tell you
to call in advance?

227
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:20,661
I did. I told you in advance
that we were coming.

228
00:10:21,495 --> 00:10:23,372
Yeah, at 6:00 p.m. yesterday!

229
00:10:23,456 --> 00:10:26,334
So I was worried
that there wouldn't be enough food.

230
00:10:26,417 --> 00:10:28,544
-It is enough.
-It's enough. It's so good.

231
00:10:28,628 --> 00:10:31,505
Now that I've met his parents, I can tell.

232
00:10:31,589 --> 00:10:34,550
-He had a very happy childhood.
-Right.

233
00:10:34,634 --> 00:10:35,551
I can feel it.

234
00:10:35,635 --> 00:10:38,346
I could tell he received
a lot of love growing up.

235
00:10:38,429 --> 00:10:40,056
-When I'd talk with him.
-Right.

236
00:10:40,139 --> 00:10:41,599
It seems he's received too much love

237
00:10:41,682 --> 00:10:44,018
so we're trying to make him
a better person.

238
00:10:44,644 --> 00:10:46,646
We noticed some things
that needed improvement.

239
00:10:48,606 --> 00:10:49,815
We're correcting them.

240
00:10:50,483 --> 00:10:52,360
That way, he can become a global star.

241
00:10:52,443 --> 00:10:53,277
Thank you.

242
00:10:53,361 --> 00:10:55,946
We're already imagining his future
three years from now.

243
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:57,823
-Right.
-We're thinking how he'll be.

244
00:10:57,907 --> 00:11:00,534
Chae-min's been sharing rooms
with him often.

245
00:11:00,618 --> 00:11:02,828
-He's keeping close tabs.
-We've slept together often.

246
00:11:02,912 --> 00:11:05,498
They have a lot in common.
Like that K-Arts paper on the fridge.

247
00:11:05,581 --> 00:11:06,749
Mine's put up at my home too.

248
00:11:06,832 --> 00:11:08,209
FAMILIAR PAPER TO A FELLOW ALUMNUS

249
00:11:08,292 --> 00:11:11,295
You still keep
the admission letter on the fridge?

250
00:11:11,379 --> 00:11:12,922
Yes, I can't throw it away.

251
00:11:13,005 --> 00:11:13,964
You just can't.

252
00:11:14,048 --> 00:11:15,341
Right, because it's K-Arts.

253
00:11:15,424 --> 00:11:19,095
Because once you print it out,
you can't print it out again.

254
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:22,765
My parents printed mine out
and laminated it.

255
00:11:22,848 --> 00:11:24,141
-Right.
-So it won't wear out.

256
00:11:24,225 --> 00:11:25,726
ADMISSION LETTER
MAJOR: MODERN DANCE

257
00:11:25,810 --> 00:11:27,853
I'm going to keep it forever.

258
00:11:27,937 --> 00:11:29,313
KOREA NATIONAL UNIVERSITY OF ARTS

259
00:11:30,231 --> 00:11:34,193
So which was
the hardest mountain to climb?

260
00:11:34,276 --> 00:11:37,988
Seoraksan. I don't even
want to pee in its direction, Dad.

261
00:11:38,072 --> 00:11:40,783
Then, I guess the Seoraksan episode
will be the longest.

262
00:11:40,866 --> 00:11:43,202
Gosh, he knows very well.

263
00:11:43,994 --> 00:11:45,454
Even his father knows very well.

264
00:11:45,538 --> 00:11:48,958
Well, I think the difficulty
should increase as you go.

265
00:11:49,041 --> 00:11:51,419
Dad!

266
00:11:51,502 --> 00:11:53,587
I thought they'd climb seven peaks a day.

267
00:11:53,671 --> 00:11:54,630
Sir!

268
00:11:54,713 --> 00:11:56,757
But you said they only hiked three peaks.

269
00:11:57,967 --> 00:11:59,260
FEELING BETRAYED

270
00:11:59,343 --> 00:12:01,303
This is what the viewers want.

271
00:12:01,387 --> 00:12:03,472
I thought he'd take our side.

272
00:12:03,556 --> 00:12:06,142
I mean, it's his son hiking.

273
00:12:06,225 --> 00:12:07,643
You know how fathers are.

274
00:12:07,726 --> 00:12:10,980
They think their sons must do
military service and go through hardships.

275
00:12:11,063 --> 00:12:15,192
We once went to the Chung-Ang University
student festival to see you.

276
00:12:15,276 --> 00:12:17,069
-You did?
-Yes, a few years ago.

277
00:12:17,153 --> 00:12:18,320
WENT TO WATCH HIM 3 YEARS AGO

278
00:12:18,404 --> 00:12:19,905
Did you have a beard back then?

279
00:12:19,989 --> 00:12:21,490
-I didn't.
-He didn't.

280
00:12:21,574 --> 00:12:23,325
-He didn't.
-It was long ago then.

281
00:12:23,409 --> 00:12:24,910
Do you like any of his songs?

282
00:12:24,994 --> 00:12:26,912
I do. My favorite is "Tree."

283
00:12:26,996 --> 00:12:28,956
-Thank you, sir.
-Sing it for him.

284
00:12:32,126 --> 00:12:34,420
PERFORMS RIGHT AWAY

285
00:12:36,547 --> 00:12:38,424
Hold on. I didn't record it.

286
00:12:39,884 --> 00:12:41,969
Could you do it again, please?

287
00:12:42,052 --> 00:12:43,137
-I'm sorry.
-All right.

288
00:12:43,846 --> 00:12:45,181
We haven't seen him sing either.

289
00:12:45,764 --> 00:12:48,058
STARTING OVER

290
00:12:52,521 --> 00:12:55,649
SINGING IN EARNEST

291
00:13:13,083 --> 00:13:14,001
That was awesome.

292
00:13:14,084 --> 00:13:16,420
He said he never sings on variety shows.

293
00:13:16,504 --> 00:13:17,546
He never sings.

294
00:13:17,630 --> 00:13:20,174
If someone's parents ask,
I do it right away.

295
00:13:20,257 --> 00:13:21,800
That was our first time hearing him.

296
00:13:21,884 --> 00:13:23,844
-Really?
-I've never seen it happen before.

297
00:13:23,928 --> 00:13:26,013
-If you come again next time…
-Of course.

298
00:13:26,096 --> 00:13:28,432
-I'll prepare a good meal for you.
-Thank you.

299
00:13:28,516 --> 00:13:32,186
After eating your food,
my fear of singing live

300
00:13:32,811 --> 00:13:34,313
just disappeared.

301
00:13:35,439 --> 00:13:36,565
It was my first time.

302
00:13:36,649 --> 00:13:38,108
-Have you heard him sing before?
-No.

303
00:13:38,192 --> 00:13:41,987
He didn't sing even when I turned on
the karaoke machine in Jeju.

304
00:13:42,071 --> 00:13:43,864
Why would I sing for you guys?

305
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:46,450
Think about it.

306
00:13:47,618 --> 00:13:50,204
After such a nice meal, how could I not?

307
00:13:50,287 --> 00:13:51,413
Today was a first.

308
00:13:52,081 --> 00:13:54,333
I came out of the bathroom right away.

309
00:13:54,416 --> 00:13:56,502
-"Why is he suddenly singing?"
-"What's happening?"

310
00:13:57,628 --> 00:13:59,004
Interesting.

311
00:13:59,088 --> 00:14:00,339
Now, I'm getting curious.

312
00:14:01,048 --> 00:14:03,175
I want to meet Chae-min's parents.

313
00:14:03,259 --> 00:14:06,512
I saw Dowoon
video calling his parents yesterday.

314
00:14:06,595 --> 00:14:09,223
Then, for Season 2,
let's visit the members' houses.

315
00:14:09,807 --> 00:14:11,100
And eat home-cooked meals.

316
00:14:11,183 --> 00:14:12,768
"Have a Home-cooked Meal!"

317
00:14:13,394 --> 00:14:14,687
That's a good idea.

318
00:14:16,313 --> 00:14:18,607
AFTER ENJOYING THE MEAL,
THEY CLEAR THE TABLE TOGETHER

319
00:14:18,691 --> 00:14:20,276
Oh, no. It's all right.

320
00:14:22,152 --> 00:14:23,028
It's not hot.

321
00:14:24,238 --> 00:14:25,114
It was really good.

322
00:14:25,197 --> 00:14:28,075
-It's been a while since I ate this much.
-Same for me.

323
00:14:28,701 --> 00:14:30,452
-This is what a meal should be.
-Right.

324
00:14:32,037 --> 00:14:33,956
We've been eating pretty well.

325
00:14:34,039 --> 00:14:36,125
-But this was so delicious.
-Right.

326
00:14:36,208 --> 00:14:38,002
THE MEAL LEFT A LASTING IMPRESSION

327
00:14:38,085 --> 00:14:39,461
The food was amazing.

328
00:14:40,504 --> 00:14:44,174
And for dessert,
this is called Ulsan <i>jjondeugi.</i>

329
00:14:45,718 --> 00:14:47,970
You make them like this. I'll put them in.

330
00:14:49,638 --> 00:14:50,639
They'll stick.

331
00:14:56,061 --> 00:14:59,148
PULLING THEM APART INTO SEPARATE STRIPS

332
00:15:01,275 --> 00:15:04,695
THE SEASONING IS A MIXTURE
OF RAMYEON SEASONING AND SUGAR

333
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:12,745
SHAKE THE JJONDEUGI WITH SEASONING
TO MIX THEM WELL, AND IT'S DONE

334
00:15:12,828 --> 00:15:13,954
Oh, that's it.

335
00:15:14,830 --> 00:15:17,750
-What's this?
-Mom, did you put on the seasoning?

336
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:19,960
I did but only put a little on purpose.

337
00:15:20,044 --> 00:15:22,004
We should add some more.

338
00:15:22,588 --> 00:15:24,757
He's being stubborn again.

339
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:28,177
There's a reason why she made it that way.

340
00:15:28,886 --> 00:15:30,679
I guess I need to discipline him more.

341
00:15:32,723 --> 00:15:34,475
Next time Tarzzan comes home,

342
00:15:34,558 --> 00:15:36,936
he'll be at the door and say,
"Mother, Father, I'm home."

343
00:15:38,270 --> 00:15:39,563
I'll teach him to do that.

344
00:15:39,647 --> 00:15:40,731
Just make him visit.

345
00:15:40,814 --> 00:15:43,609
Okay, I'll send him here
by courier service.

346
00:15:44,526 --> 00:15:46,111
Use your hands to rip them apart.

347
00:15:46,195 --> 00:15:48,364
TARZZAN'S MOM'S ULSAN JJONDEUGI

348
00:15:49,239 --> 00:15:51,116
I see. Eating it this way is good too.

349
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:52,785
There's a seasoning for this?

350
00:15:54,244 --> 00:15:55,996
It's good.

351
00:15:56,747 --> 00:15:57,915
You can't stop eating it.

352
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:02,962
After school,
there was no better snack than this.

353
00:16:03,045 --> 00:16:04,505
IT FILLS TARZZAN WITH NOSTALGIA

354
00:16:05,464 --> 00:16:07,257
SHE EVEN PREPARED CAKES AND FRUITS

355
00:16:07,341 --> 00:16:09,593
-One per person?
-Thank you.

356
00:16:09,677 --> 00:16:11,553
Gosh, the presentation.

357
00:16:11,637 --> 00:16:13,639
1 PLATE PER PERSON

358
00:16:13,722 --> 00:16:16,225
You should take a photo
and share it on your social media.

359
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:20,270
You can title it as "Tarzzan-kase."

360
00:16:21,563 --> 00:16:23,774
I think we should go hiking right now.

361
00:16:23,857 --> 00:16:24,942
Because of the calories.

362
00:16:25,025 --> 00:16:26,235
EQUALS CALORIES FOR 3 PEAKS

363
00:16:26,318 --> 00:16:27,861
Thank her with a deep bow after we go.

364
00:16:27,945 --> 00:16:28,904
Okay.

365
00:16:29,738 --> 00:16:31,115
-For real?
-Yes, for real.

366
00:16:32,116 --> 00:16:33,993
Has the next mountain been decided yet?

367
00:16:34,076 --> 00:16:35,369
-It has.
-It has.

368
00:16:36,286 --> 00:16:37,496
It's Jirisan.

369
00:16:38,038 --> 00:16:39,206
Oh no!

370
00:16:39,790 --> 00:16:42,167
Seriously, ma'am, once you watch the show,

371
00:16:42,251 --> 00:16:44,336
you'll hate Producer Nah.

372
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:45,504
It'll break your heart.

373
00:16:45,587 --> 00:16:46,922
Oh no.

374
00:16:49,341 --> 00:16:51,760
SHE ALWAYS WORRIES ABOUT HER ONLY SON

375
00:16:51,844 --> 00:16:53,929
-It's really tough.
-Tell him no.

376
00:16:54,013 --> 00:16:55,180
Please tell him no.

377
00:16:55,889 --> 00:16:57,266
I'm sorry.

378
00:16:59,018 --> 00:17:00,060
I wanted to hear this.

379
00:17:00,144 --> 00:17:02,479
-Finally, someone's taking our side.
-Finally.

380
00:17:02,563 --> 00:17:04,023
She's the first adult on our side.

381
00:17:04,106 --> 00:17:05,816
I've been waiting for so long.

382
00:17:05,899 --> 00:17:08,110
Have you learned anything?

383
00:17:09,236 --> 00:17:10,237
No.

384
00:17:11,780 --> 00:17:13,615
-Nothing at all.
-Really?

385
00:17:13,699 --> 00:17:16,243
But on the Yeongnam Alps yesterday…

386
00:17:16,326 --> 00:17:19,455
I thought it was nice
for the very first time. It was beautiful.

387
00:17:19,538 --> 00:17:21,915
The weather was nice, and it wasn't snowy.

388
00:17:21,999 --> 00:17:25,544
You know, we had always hiked
snowy mountains before that.

389
00:17:25,627 --> 00:17:27,463
But it wasn't snowy yesterday.

390
00:17:27,546 --> 00:17:29,965
-Now that we've eaten a lot of food…
-Right.

391
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:31,050
I think we should go

392
00:17:31,133 --> 00:17:34,428
so that Tarzzan can spend
some time with his parents.

393
00:17:34,511 --> 00:17:35,554
All right.

394
00:17:36,388 --> 00:17:38,599
-Thank you for the food.
-Thank you so much.

395
00:17:39,349 --> 00:17:41,435
-Thank you for coming.
-Thank you.

396
00:17:42,352 --> 00:17:45,481
Before we go, I should tell you
I thought you were his sister at first.

397
00:17:45,564 --> 00:17:46,774
Thank you!

398
00:17:47,524 --> 00:17:48,609
You look so young.

399
00:17:48,692 --> 00:17:50,611
Darn, you beat me to it.

400
00:17:51,945 --> 00:17:53,113
Bye, sis.

401
00:17:55,074 --> 00:17:56,742
-See you later, guys.
-Goodbye.

402
00:17:56,825 --> 00:17:57,951
Bye.

403
00:17:58,035 --> 00:17:59,703
-Bye. Thank you.
-Thank you.

404
00:17:59,787 --> 00:18:00,704
Goodbye.

405
00:18:00,788 --> 00:18:02,498
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

406
00:18:02,581 --> 00:18:03,749
-Bye.
-Keep in touch.

407
00:18:03,832 --> 00:18:05,084
-Thank you.
-Bye.

408
00:18:05,167 --> 00:18:06,668
DESCEND CLUB'S
ULSAN EXPEDITION ENDS

409
00:18:06,752 --> 00:18:08,337
THANK YOU FOR THE MEAL, TARZZAN

410
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:09,922
IT WAS THE BEST

411
00:18:10,005 --> 00:18:11,632
SAY THANKS TO YOUR PARENTS AND AUNT

412
00:18:11,715 --> 00:18:13,175
THANKS FOR COMING, GUYS

413
00:18:13,258 --> 00:18:14,802
DID YOU BOW TO THEM YET?

414
00:18:14,885 --> 00:18:16,887
I DID AND HERE'S THE PROOF!

415
00:18:23,227 --> 00:18:25,270
A MONTH LATER

416
00:18:25,979 --> 00:18:28,065
AS SPRING DEEPENS IN MARCH

417
00:18:29,024 --> 00:18:31,485
AND THE LONG WINTER
MELTS AWAY LITTLE BY LITTLE

418
00:18:32,402 --> 00:18:34,905
DESCEND CLUB'S LAST HIKE
IS JUST A DAY AWAY

419
00:18:35,823 --> 00:18:38,283
IT'S TIME TO LEAVE NOW

420
00:18:38,367 --> 00:18:40,828
FOR JIRISAN

421
00:18:40,911 --> 00:18:42,621
SEOUL MANNAMUI GWANGJANG SERVICE AREA

422
00:18:42,704 --> 00:18:44,248
EXPRESSWAY REST STOP

423
00:18:47,584 --> 00:18:49,461
THEY'LL MEET HERE AND LEAVE TOGETHER

424
00:18:55,717 --> 00:18:57,094
TAKE A HIKE!

425
00:18:57,177 --> 00:18:59,680
VIP SERVICE FOR JIRISAN

426
00:18:59,763 --> 00:19:01,348
Car-the is here. Hello.

427
00:19:01,431 --> 00:19:02,766
CAR, THE GARDEN ARRIVES FIRST

428
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:04,518
-Hi.
-Do we need crampons?

429
00:19:05,102 --> 00:19:07,104
Yes. I think we'll need them.

430
00:19:07,187 --> 00:19:10,107
It's still snowy at high altitudes.

431
00:19:11,108 --> 00:19:12,609
Does anyone take pills for hair loss?

432
00:19:13,110 --> 00:19:13,944
Why?

433
00:19:14,027 --> 00:19:16,196
Didn't the hair on the top of my head

434
00:19:17,239 --> 00:19:18,866
look less dense on camera?

435
00:19:18,949 --> 00:19:20,534
I didn't notice it at all.

436
00:19:20,617 --> 00:19:22,244
-Isn't there enough?
-The top of my head…

437
00:19:22,327 --> 00:19:23,370
THE CAMERA SUDDENLY RISES

438
00:19:23,453 --> 00:19:24,371
It's starting to thin.

439
00:19:24,454 --> 00:19:26,165
Why are you filming that?

440
00:19:26,999 --> 00:19:30,460
Right now, I have some product on.

441
00:19:31,628 --> 00:19:33,005
From Etude House…

442
00:19:34,756 --> 00:19:36,216
I put that on my hair.

443
00:19:37,050 --> 00:19:38,385
Hello.

444
00:19:38,468 --> 00:19:40,470
-How have you been?
-Good.

445
00:19:40,554 --> 00:19:41,513
CHAE-MIN SOON ARRIVES

446
00:19:41,597 --> 00:19:42,806
I think you've lost weight.

447
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:45,392
I've been on a diet. I run these days.

448
00:19:45,475 --> 00:19:46,518
-Running?
-Yes.

449
00:19:46,602 --> 00:19:48,228
To hike better?

450
00:19:48,312 --> 00:19:49,354
GLARES

451
00:19:49,438 --> 00:19:50,480
TURNS INTO A TYRANT

452
00:19:50,564 --> 00:19:52,024
I've forgotten what this feels like.

453
00:19:54,151 --> 00:19:56,195
THEY WAIT FOR DOWOON AND TARZZAN
ON THE BUS

454
00:19:56,862 --> 00:19:58,197
Hello, Jung-won.

455
00:19:58,280 --> 00:19:59,698
You look cool today.

456
00:19:59,781 --> 00:20:03,160
This is the last one.
I thought I should dress for the occasion.

457
00:20:03,243 --> 00:20:06,079
I was wondering why you guys
seemed to be in a good mood.

458
00:20:06,163 --> 00:20:07,956
It was because this is the last one.

459
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:09,917
The bus is nice too.

460
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,252
THEY'RE MORE CHEERFUL THAN USUAL

461
00:20:12,336 --> 00:20:14,755
How long is the round-trip hike
for Jirisan?

462
00:20:14,838 --> 00:20:17,716
It's about nine to ten hours.

463
00:20:17,799 --> 00:20:19,009
How hard is it?

464
00:20:19,092 --> 00:20:21,470
He's already showing
an interest in the hike.

465
00:20:21,553 --> 00:20:23,096
How should I put it?

466
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:25,766
Car-the is so passionate.

467
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:30,395
You know what I found so funny
about myself?

468
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:31,772
My close friends

469
00:20:31,855 --> 00:20:35,275
suggested that we go hike
Gwanaksan Mountain.

470
00:20:35,359 --> 00:20:37,694
But I acted arrogant.

471
00:20:37,778 --> 00:20:39,947
HE'S A TRUE HIKER NOW

472
00:20:40,030 --> 00:20:41,406
Tarzzan has just arrived.

473
00:20:41,490 --> 00:20:42,532
Is Tarzzan here?

474
00:20:42,616 --> 00:20:43,617
TARZZAN ARRIVES

475
00:20:44,451 --> 00:20:45,535
AND DOWOON TOO

476
00:20:45,619 --> 00:20:47,287
-You look happy.
-Hello.

477
00:20:47,371 --> 00:20:49,623
-Chae-won, long time no see.
-Dowoon.

478
00:20:51,750 --> 00:20:53,794
-It's been a while.
-Let's never hike again.

479
00:20:54,711 --> 00:20:56,546
You must've been dying to go hiking.

480
00:20:56,630 --> 00:20:58,840
-This is the last one.
-I know, right?

481
00:20:59,841 --> 00:21:01,093
How have you been?

482
00:21:01,176 --> 00:21:03,804
Well, I've been waiting for today.

483
00:21:04,846 --> 00:21:07,641
I'm sure the production crew
has been eager for this day too.

484
00:21:09,935 --> 00:21:12,104
ENTERING CONFIDENTLY

485
00:21:12,187 --> 00:21:13,605
This is the last one!

486
00:21:14,231 --> 00:21:16,400
HE CAN'T HIDE HIS EXCITEMENT

487
00:21:16,483 --> 00:21:18,568
Hey, it's the last one.

488
00:21:18,652 --> 00:21:20,153
THE LAST HELLO TO THE SOUND MIXER

489
00:21:20,237 --> 00:21:21,947
He looks so excited.

490
00:21:22,531 --> 00:21:24,491
-Hey.
-Hi, Jung-won.

491
00:21:25,742 --> 00:21:28,662
EVERYONE'S GATHERED IN A GOOD MOOD

492
00:21:28,745 --> 00:21:30,539
Why am I so upbeat today?

493
00:21:30,622 --> 00:21:32,332
Gosh, I'm so corny!

494
00:21:34,084 --> 00:21:36,920
What time will we start tomorrow?
Will you tell us now?

495
00:21:37,004 --> 00:21:40,424
We're thinking of leaving at 6:00 a.m.

496
00:21:40,507 --> 00:21:42,175
But that's a bit too early.

497
00:21:42,259 --> 00:21:43,927
Come on, it's not that early.

498
00:21:44,594 --> 00:21:47,014
-So it takes about nine hours?
-Yes.

499
00:21:47,097 --> 00:21:49,266
IT'S GOING TO BE A LONG HIKE YET AGAIN

500
00:21:49,349 --> 00:21:50,434
It's about average.

501
