answers to that quickly.

731
00:33:47,108 --> 00:33:48,609
A lot faster than hiking?

732
00:33:48,693 --> 00:33:49,861
HE LIKES TRAVELING

733
00:33:49,944 --> 00:33:51,863
I see. What about Car-the?

734
00:33:51,946 --> 00:33:52,822
What I want to do?

735
00:33:52,905 --> 00:33:54,657
-Just off the top of my head?
-Yes.

736
00:33:54,741 --> 00:33:56,117
I just want to rest and hang out.

737
00:33:58,036 --> 00:33:59,537
<i>Take a Rest and Hang Out!</i>

738
00:33:59,620 --> 00:34:00,913
For the rest of your life?

739
00:34:00,997 --> 00:34:02,290
I just want to hang out.

740
00:34:02,373 --> 00:34:05,960
To tell you the truth,
except for the hiking,

741
00:34:06,044 --> 00:34:07,128
I really like this show.

742
00:34:08,171 --> 00:34:10,590
A HIKING SHOW WITHOUT HIKING IS GOOD

743
00:34:10,673 --> 00:34:12,341
I think this would be good.

744
00:34:12,425 --> 00:34:15,511
<i>Take a Rest in Bed and Stay Home!</i>

745
00:34:15,595 --> 00:34:16,429
Something like that.

746
00:34:16,512 --> 00:34:18,347
THE MINISTER OF TRANSPORT
DOESN'T WANT TO MOVE

747
00:34:18,431 --> 00:34:21,476
Anyway, if you happen to reach 100 km,

748
00:34:21,559 --> 00:34:24,353
we'll do one of the things you guys want

749
00:34:24,437 --> 00:34:25,688
in the next season.

750
00:34:25,772 --> 00:34:27,482
But I don't think
100 km was ever possible.

751
00:34:27,565 --> 00:34:29,108
Then, you can't keep your promise.

752
00:34:29,734 --> 00:34:32,487
So we're going to give you the last chance

753
00:34:32,570 --> 00:34:34,864
-to reach 100 km.
-What?

754
00:34:34,947 --> 00:34:36,741
Once again, like last time,

755
00:34:36,824 --> 00:34:38,951
we'll play a simple game
wagering kilometers.

756
00:34:39,035 --> 00:34:41,662
We're giving you a chance
to reach 100 km today.

757
00:34:41,746 --> 00:34:43,790
Damn it!

758
00:34:45,625 --> 00:34:48,961
<i>If you earn 30 km today,</i>
<i>we'll do the type of show you want.</i>

759
00:34:49,045 --> 00:34:51,798
<i>If you don't, Season 2 will also be…</i>

760
00:34:51,881 --> 00:34:54,926
HIKING AGAIN

761
00:34:55,009 --> 00:34:57,220
But we have nothing to lose.

762
00:34:57,303 --> 00:34:58,930
We're already at 70 km anyway,

763
00:34:59,013 --> 00:35:02,100
and today's the last day,
so it doesn't matter if we lose it all.

764
00:35:02,183 --> 00:35:03,351
This is true.

765
00:35:03,935 --> 00:35:05,228
We're offering you a good deal.

766
00:35:05,311 --> 00:35:06,145
Okay.

767
00:35:06,229 --> 00:35:09,273
Last time, if you bet 1 km,
the return was 1 km.

768
00:35:09,357 --> 00:35:11,776
We'll double the return this time.

769
00:35:11,859 --> 00:35:13,611
If you bet 1 km, you can earn 2 km.

770
00:35:13,694 --> 00:35:16,155
If you bet 5 km, you can earn 10 km.

771
00:35:16,239 --> 00:35:18,825
If you bet 10 km, you can earn 20 km.

772
00:35:18,908 --> 00:35:21,494
If we lose, we give away 10 km.
But if we win, we get 20 km?

773
00:35:21,577 --> 00:35:23,788
Yes, that's right. It's such a great deal.

774
00:35:23,871 --> 00:35:26,457
-But the game must not be easy.
-Right.

775
00:35:26,541 --> 00:35:30,211
-Then, can I tell you about the game?
-Yes.

776
00:35:30,294 --> 00:35:32,171
I don't feel confident though.

777
00:35:32,880 --> 00:35:34,549
MR. KIM UI-HAN IS WORRIED

778
00:35:34,632 --> 00:35:36,551
Dowoon likes this game so much.

779
00:35:36,634 --> 00:35:37,635
-He's good.
-Right.

780
00:35:37,718 --> 00:35:39,637
Let's play "Finish the Phrase."

781
00:35:39,720 --> 00:35:42,223
We're going to lose everything today.

782
00:35:42,306 --> 00:35:44,559
UI-HAN LOOKS SAD

783
00:35:44,642 --> 00:35:45,643
The category is

784
00:35:45,726 --> 00:35:47,520
proverbs.

785
00:35:47,603 --> 00:35:49,313
-I'm not good with proverbs.
-Proverbs…

786
00:35:50,064 --> 00:35:52,024
THE YOUNGER MEMBERS
ARE SURPRISINGLY NOT CONFIDENT

787
00:35:52,108 --> 00:35:53,609
I really don't know any proverbs.

788
00:35:53,693 --> 00:35:54,819
I'm really bad with them.

789
00:35:54,902 --> 00:35:56,487
You can practice. Start with Car-the.

790
00:35:56,571 --> 00:35:58,406
-Kill two birds…
-With one stone.

791
00:35:59,282 --> 00:36:00,449
Yes, like that.

792
00:36:00,533 --> 00:36:02,285
-Get two for…
-Trimming branches.

793
00:36:03,244 --> 00:36:04,996
-What was that, Dowoon?
-Trimming branches.

794
00:36:05,079 --> 00:36:07,165
-"Trimming cheese"?
-Trimming branches.

795
00:36:07,248 --> 00:36:09,041
-Trimming branches.
-"Trimming branches"?

796
00:36:09,125 --> 00:36:10,501
A PROVERB FOR PLANT OWNERS

797
00:36:10,585 --> 00:36:13,212
Hold on, stop it. Save it for later.

798
00:36:13,296 --> 00:36:14,130
That was funny.

799
00:36:14,213 --> 00:36:15,381
ON ANOTHER LEVEL AGAIN TODAY

800
00:36:15,464 --> 00:36:17,049
Get two for what?

801
00:36:17,133 --> 00:36:17,967
FOR THE PRICE OF ONE

802
00:36:18,050 --> 00:36:18,885
Trimming branches?

803
00:36:19,510 --> 00:36:20,469
This is a big problem.

804
00:36:20,553 --> 00:36:21,929
You and I didn't know.

805
00:36:22,013 --> 00:36:23,306
Right, I didn't know either.

806
00:36:23,389 --> 00:36:24,515
AN UNEXPECTED VARIABLE

807
00:36:24,599 --> 00:36:25,516
What's funny is,

808
00:36:25,600 --> 00:36:27,351
young people don't know
proverbs these days.

809
00:36:27,435 --> 00:36:28,978
-We don't.
-Of course not.

810
00:36:29,061 --> 00:36:30,813
So close…

811
00:36:30,897 --> 00:36:32,607
So close?

812
00:36:33,107 --> 00:36:34,400
It was something about distance.

813
00:36:35,151 --> 00:36:36,277
And almost there?

814
00:36:36,360 --> 00:36:37,737
They're really bad.

815
00:36:37,820 --> 00:36:39,322
I'm really bad with proverbs.

816
00:36:39,405 --> 00:36:41,407
So close, yet so far.

817
00:36:42,742 --> 00:36:44,202
How much will you bet?

818
00:36:44,285 --> 00:36:46,287
-This is the first round.
-We'll bet 0.5 km.

819
00:36:47,163 --> 00:36:48,748
A DROP IN THE OCEAN

820
00:36:48,831 --> 00:36:51,125
Hey, we'll definitely lose.

821
00:36:51,209 --> 00:36:52,835
So, 0.5 km.

822
00:36:52,919 --> 00:36:54,003
You're betting 0.5 km?

823
00:36:54,086 --> 00:36:55,838
AN EMBARRASSING AMOUNT

824
00:36:55,922 --> 00:36:57,924
Yes, we'll bet 0.5.

825
00:36:58,633 --> 00:36:59,967
It's because…

826
00:37:01,093 --> 00:37:02,803
We have our reasons.

827
00:37:02,887 --> 00:37:05,097
So please be understanding.

828
00:37:05,181 --> 00:37:07,391
-So you'll bet 0.5 km?
-Yes.

829
00:37:07,475 --> 00:37:09,101
Still, we can earn 1 km if we win.

830
00:37:09,185 --> 00:37:11,812
Okay, we'll start off simple
and bet 0.5 km.

831
00:37:11,896 --> 00:37:12,980
Shall we start?

832
00:37:13,064 --> 00:37:14,982
With 0.5 km on the line,
is Car-the going first?

833
00:37:15,066 --> 00:37:16,359
-Yes.
-It's for 0.5 km.

834
00:37:16,442 --> 00:37:17,568
All right.

835
00:37:17,652 --> 00:37:19,612
Do you want to switch seats with me?

836
00:37:19,695 --> 00:37:23,366
Do you want just one turn?
I am still a bit older than you, so…

837
00:37:24,033 --> 00:37:26,327
SWITCHING SEATS

838
00:37:26,410 --> 00:37:27,703
I'm counting on you, Dowoon.

839
00:37:27,787 --> 00:37:28,663
Here we go.

840
00:37:28,746 --> 00:37:30,623
It'd be better for us to switch too.

841
00:37:30,706 --> 00:37:32,250
Getting at least two right's better.

842
00:37:32,333 --> 00:37:34,001
SWITCHING SEATS

843
00:37:35,002 --> 00:37:37,672
Since the category is proverbs,
it's in order of age now.

844
00:37:38,422 --> 00:37:41,092
-Are you ready?
-I was looking back on my life.

845
00:37:41,175 --> 00:37:43,261
Proverbs usually come
from life experiences.

846
00:37:44,387 --> 00:37:46,973
THEY ONLY GET 10 CHANCES

847
00:37:47,056 --> 00:37:48,474
Okay, let's go.

848
00:37:48,557 --> 00:37:50,685
BETTING 0.5 KM

849
00:37:50,768 --> 00:37:52,019
Okay, here come the proverbs.

850
00:37:53,271 --> 00:37:54,605
As you sow…

851
00:37:54,689 --> 00:37:56,440
-So shall you reap.
-Correct!

852
00:37:58,276 --> 00:37:59,735
Bad news…

853
00:37:59,819 --> 00:38:01,696
-Travels fast.
-Correct!

854
00:38:01,779 --> 00:38:02,697
Hold on.

855
00:38:05,491 --> 00:38:07,034
Appearances can be…

856
00:38:07,118 --> 00:38:08,494
-Deceiving.
-Correct!

857
00:38:08,577 --> 00:38:09,662
Very good.

858
00:38:09,745 --> 00:38:11,080
Where there's smoke…

859
00:38:11,956 --> 00:38:13,416
-There's Santa Claus.
-Wrong!

860
00:38:14,333 --> 00:38:15,334
Hey, come on!

861
00:38:15,418 --> 00:38:16,585
-There's Santa Claus.
-Wrong!

862
00:38:16,669 --> 00:38:17,962
SANTA CLAUS?

863
00:38:18,045 --> 00:38:19,005
Hey, come on!

864
00:38:19,588 --> 00:38:22,174
Hey, it's about proverbs!

865
00:38:22,258 --> 00:38:23,175
Proverbs.

866
00:38:23,259 --> 00:38:24,802
What kind of proverb has Santa Claus?

867
00:38:24,885 --> 00:38:28,222
I know Netflix is headquartered
in another country,

868
00:38:28,306 --> 00:38:29,348
but it's a Korean proverb.

869
00:38:29,432 --> 00:38:31,600
How could you say "Santa Claus"?

870
00:38:31,684 --> 00:38:34,228
Wait, what's the answer?
Where there's smoke…

871
00:38:35,271 --> 00:38:36,939
-There's fire.
-There's fire.

872
00:38:37,690 --> 00:38:38,983
I'm doing pretty well.

873
00:38:39,066 --> 00:38:41,235
The older members are a bit better.

874
00:38:41,319 --> 00:38:43,571
THE YOUNGEST FEELS
MORE AND MORE EMBARRASSED

875
00:38:43,654 --> 00:38:45,364
Smoke usually comes from a chimney,

876
00:38:45,448 --> 00:38:47,742
so you thought of Santa Claus?

877
00:38:47,825 --> 00:38:48,784
I'm pretty imaginative.

878
00:38:48,868 --> 00:38:50,161
SMOKE TO CHIMNEY TO SANTA CLAUS

879
00:38:50,244 --> 00:38:52,621
I do understand where he's coming from.

880
00:38:52,705 --> 00:38:55,333
IF YOU THINK ABOUT IT, IT'S KIND OF CUTE

881
00:38:55,416 --> 00:38:58,919
Now, you have lost 0.5 km each.

882
00:38:59,003 --> 00:38:59,879
LAUGHS

883
00:38:59,962 --> 00:39:01,464
It's good that we only bet 0.5.

884
00:39:01,547 --> 00:39:02,673
Okay, good.

885
00:39:02,757 --> 00:39:03,841
WISE CHOICE

886
00:39:03,924 --> 00:39:05,384
-Will you bet 0.5 km again?
-Yes.

887
00:39:05,468 --> 00:39:07,511
-Just 0.5.
-Come on, let's go big.

888
00:39:07,595 --> 00:39:09,305
Let's go with 0.7. then.

889
00:39:10,389 --> 00:39:13,809
Hey, 0.7 makes us look a bit petty.

890
00:39:13,893 --> 00:39:15,603
-It looks bad.
-Okay, make it 1 km.

891
00:39:15,686 --> 00:39:16,937
"It looks bad."

892
00:39:17,855 --> 00:39:19,273
Betting 0.7 is ridiculous.

893
00:39:19,357 --> 00:39:20,691
So, 1 km then?

894
00:39:20,775 --> 00:39:21,942
-Yes.
-Yes, 1 km.

895
00:39:22,026 --> 00:39:23,319
Okay, we'll speed things up.

896
00:39:23,402 --> 00:39:24,987
There will be no pauses this time.

897
00:39:25,071 --> 00:39:26,155
Car-the will go first.

898
00:39:27,031 --> 00:39:28,449
Experience is the best…

899
00:39:28,532 --> 00:39:30,076
-Teacher.
-Correct.

900
00:39:30,159 --> 00:39:31,243
Betrayal comes from those…

901
00:39:31,327 --> 00:39:32,578
-You trust the most.
-Correct.

902
00:39:32,661 --> 00:39:34,205
You can spot potential…

903
00:39:34,288 --> 00:39:35,831
-I don't know this.
-Wrong!

904
00:39:36,749 --> 00:39:38,417
-You've never heard of it before?
-Never.

905
00:39:38,501 --> 00:39:39,794
"You can spot potential"?

906
00:39:39,877 --> 00:39:41,837
At an early age.

907
00:39:42,588 --> 00:39:43,589
He's good.

908
00:39:43,672 --> 00:39:44,632
But it does make sense.

909
00:39:44,715 --> 00:39:47,343
From an early age,
you can see one's potential.

910
00:39:47,426 --> 00:39:48,552
UNDERSTANDS AFTER HEARING IT

911
00:39:48,636 --> 00:39:49,887
Potential?

912
00:39:49,970 --> 00:39:52,098
Young people really don't use
proverbs these days.

913
00:39:52,181 --> 00:39:53,099
HE DIDN'T KNOW

914
00:39:53,182 --> 00:39:54,683
We lost 1 km?

915
00:39:54,767 --> 00:39:56,519
We won't win anything at this rate.

916
00:39:56,602 --> 00:39:59,355
Even if it's a one-way trip,
I don't think they'll succeed.

917
00:39:59,438 --> 00:40:00,439
Probably not.

918
00:40:00,523 --> 00:40:02,441
Hold on. If it's one-way, maybe…

919
00:40:03,859 --> 00:40:05,528
You can't take back what you say.

920
00:40:05,611 --> 00:40:06,987
What?

921
00:40:07,071 --> 00:40:08,155
One successful pass counts.

922
00:40:08,239 --> 00:40:09,657
-Was that a proverb just now?
-Yes.

923
00:40:09,740 --> 00:40:11,325
"You can't take back what you say."

924
00:40:11,909 --> 00:40:12,827
A GENIUS WITH PROVERBS

925
00:40:12,910 --> 00:40:13,869
-Really?
-You said one.

926
00:40:13,953 --> 00:40:16,747
It's no use crying over spilled milk.

927
00:40:17,873 --> 00:40:19,875
-Let's try a one-way trip.
-Let's do it.

928
00:40:19,959 --> 00:40:21,585
How much will you bet?

929
00:40:21,669 --> 00:40:23,003
-Let's bet big.
-Maybe 2 km?

930
00:40:23,087 --> 00:40:24,755
-Hold on. No.
-Are you confident?

931
00:40:25,381 --> 00:40:26,715
-Then, 3 km?
-3 km?

932
00:40:27,299 --> 00:40:28,926
Are you confident? Tarzzan?

933
00:40:29,009 --> 00:40:31,637
I'm not confident at all.
I'm telling you in advance.

934
00:40:31,720 --> 00:40:33,305
STRENGTHS
I'M HONEST

935
00:40:33,389 --> 00:40:34,557
-Then, let's bet 2 km.
-2 km?

936
00:40:34,640 --> 00:40:36,142
Just in case because it's one pass.

937
00:40:36,225 --> 00:40:37,977
Let's bet 2 km, and you go first.

938
00:40:38,602 --> 00:40:39,520
You go first.

939
00:40:39,603 --> 00:40:41,730
It's better if you get it over with first.

940
00:40:41,814 --> 00:40:44,150
-Okay.
-If you fail, we can move on right away.

941
00:40:44,233 --> 00:40:45,526
LOW EXPECTATIONS

942
00:40:45,609 --> 00:40:47,611
Tarzzan, I believe in you.

943
00:40:47,695 --> 00:40:48,779
BETTING 2 KM

944
00:40:48,863 --> 00:40:50,698
Okay, here we go. Tarzzan will go first.

945
00:40:52,533 --> 00:40:54,118
What goes around…

946
00:40:54,201 --> 00:40:55,453
Comes around.

947
00:40:55,536 --> 00:40:56,454
Correct!

948
00:40:58,372 --> 00:40:59,999
A chest feeling fear…

949
00:41:00,875 --> 00:41:03,002
Chae-min. A chest feeling fear…

950
00:41:03,919 --> 00:41:05,838
-Three, two…
-Gets bigger!

951
00:41:05,921 --> 00:41:06,797
Wrong!

952
00:41:08,924 --> 00:41:10,384
-Gets bigger!
-Wrong!

953
00:41:12,595 --> 00:41:15,097
A TOTALLY UNEXPECTED WRONG ANSWER

954
00:41:15,181 --> 00:41:16,599
What gets bigger?

955
00:41:16,682 --> 00:41:19,059
Hey, what do you mean "chest gets bigger"?

956
00:41:19,560 --> 00:41:21,645
SILENT

957
00:41:21,729 --> 00:41:24,857
Why would you say "chest gets bigger"?

958
00:41:24,940 --> 00:41:26,358
-Geez, Chae-min.
-Chae-min.

959
00:41:26,442 --> 00:41:28,152
VERY FLUSTERED

960
00:41:28,235 --> 00:41:29,737
You said "filling up," so…

961
00:41:30,863 --> 00:41:32,948
-"Filling up."
-You heard "filling up"?

962
00:41:33,032 --> 00:41:34,617
"Filling up"!

963
00:41:34,700 --> 00:41:36,160
"A chest filling up"!

964
00:41:36,243 --> 00:41:39,079
HE HEARD "A CHEST FEELING FEAR"
AS "A CHEST FILLING UP"

965
00:41:39,163 --> 00:41:40,831
Didn't he say "filling up"?

966
00:41:40,915 --> 00:41:43,876
It was "feeling," not "filling."

967
00:41:44,752 --> 00:41:46,879
OH, NO…

968
00:41:46,962 --> 00:41:49,089
You said, "A chest feeling fear"?

969
00:41:49,173 --> 00:41:50,633
I heard it as, "A chest filling up."

970
00:41:50,716 --> 00:41:51,967
FEELING WRONGED

971
00:41:52,051 --> 00:41:54,553
Hold on. Did anyone know the answer?

972
00:41:56,013 --> 00:41:58,432
Is it related to pirate tales
or something?

973
00:41:58,516 --> 00:42:00,893
CHESTS TO PIRATE TALES

974
00:42:02,228 --> 00:42:04,396
So, what's the answer?

975
00:42:04,480 --> 00:42:05,731
"It's easily startled again."

976
00:42:06,982 --> 00:42:08,692
"A chest filled with fear"?

977
00:42:08,776 --> 00:42:11,987
If something scared you before,
seeing it again would startle you.

978
00:42:12,071 --> 00:42:13,822
Like, "Oh my goodness!"

979
00:42:13,906 --> 00:42:16,450
It's like the idiom
"once bitten, twice shy."

980
00:42:17,159 --> 00:42:19,286
Isn't this a pronunciation problem then?

981
00:42:19,370 --> 00:42:23,249
What are you talking about?
You two understood perfectly well.

982
00:42:23,332 --> 00:42:24,875
ANYWAY…

983
00:42:24,959 --> 00:42:28,921
Could you make sure to edit this?
I think it's going to look bad.

984
00:42:32,925 --> 00:42:34,552
SINCE THEY'RE MUCH WORSE THAN EXPECTED…

985
00:42:34,635 --> 00:42:37,429
This is worse than we thought.

986
00:42:37,513 --> 00:42:39,890
-The category Tarzzan was confident in.
-What was it?

987
00:42:39,974 --> 00:42:42,142
-Should we try brands?
-Brands? Okay.

988
00:42:42,226 --> 00:42:43,727
Not just any brand

989
00:42:43,811 --> 00:42:45,646
but snacks or ice cream brands.

990
00:42:45,729 --> 00:42:47,022
I'm confident with food.

991
00:42:47,106 --> 00:42:48,107
CONFIDENT

992
00:42:48,190 --> 00:42:49,066
I like eating.

993
00:42:49,149 --> 00:42:51,694
For example, Shrimp…

994
00:42:51,777 --> 00:42:52,778
Crackers.

995
00:42:52,861 --> 00:42:54,446
-Product names? Okay.
-Yes.

996
00:42:54,530 --> 00:42:57,157
All right, snacks and ice cream.
How much will you bet?

997
00:42:57,783 --> 00:42:59,702
-Let's try 1 km.
-One or two? One?

998
00:43:00,369 --> 00:43:01,453
Maybe 2 km?

